          "heading": "Geological framework: questions, scales and competing evidence",
          "content": "A source-to-sink approach connects hillslope weathering, river delivery, shelf storage, canyon bypass, basin-floor transport and burial. Fluxes need common units and time windows. A single sediment trap measures one location, not total transport; a core measures surviving deposits, not all historical flow events. Event layers may dominate a section even when quiet periods dominate the elapsed time. Reworking transfers old particles into young deposits, so the age of a grain is not necessarily the age of deposition. Basin morphology alters where a flow accelerates, deposits and escapes into adjacent basins. These explanations must be tested with facies sequences, cross-sectional geometry and sediment provenance, not a single spectacular acoustic image.",
